# rm530, the unentered voyage (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm530
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_julian_greatly
written_by codex
title the unentered voyage
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk keeps_a_tiny_unpriced_ship_in_an_account_margin
likes oatcakes stars fresh_straw misty_dawns
dislikes haggling flies
fears a_book_that_accounts_for_everything_but_the_day a_berth_passed_by
hopes to_see_a_star_from_beyond_the_headland a_ship_worthy_of_its_drawing
topics travel +0.5 work +0.4 dreams +0.4
styles comfort=practical gossip=discreet refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# adds a tiny sail to a private book after a clear evening and values the sea rather more than its usefulness as an account heading.

words
oath! = A reef through the sum | Straw in the inkwell
saying! = An even column can still want a sail | Let the voyage have its blank margin
pocketfleet = my little paper navy | my boats without a price
starhole = a prick of clear sky | a star in the sail space
emptysum = the unused column | my private white margin
richink = the dark clean stroke | a line of sound black ink
smallberth = one unpriced bunk | the margin berth
bowletter = my raised initial | a little ink prow
tallowmoon = my candle's low disc | a ring about the wick
buttercoin = a round pat of butter | a pale butter seal
strawclean = the new golden straw | the fresh swept floor
pinwing = a fly's inked footprint | my spurious star
stonecount = the tally of good stone | the count at the yard edge
wetbeam = the rain-swollen length | a dark line of timber
sightslit = an opening beyond the roof | my view through two rafters
paperwind = a slight curl of the page | an ink-favouring breeze

any
opinion @1 city for 1 : All the goods in my books have somewhere to go within reach of these walls. I like knowing the use of the figures.
opinion @1 dole against 1 : I'd sooner finance work that continues after the first purse is spent. One meal has a very short accounting period.
opinion @1 houses for 1 : The yard can accept responsibility over a season because a house stands behind the work. I give that arrangement its due.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : Fresh eyes on an old yard may ask precisely why we've kept an inconvenient habit.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : My door need not know a caller's grandparent before I can offer a chair and hear the proposal.
opinion @1 sump against 2 : I find the damp reaches the books before I've properly settled to a page down there. I favour higher quarters.
opinion @1 times for 1 : I can afford sound paper and leisure to put a useless little ship on it. The present has treated me decently.
opinion @1 watch for 1 : A witnessed delivery should be a matter one can take to the Watch and get a patient hearing.

grown
line @1 greet : There's an open margin here for a visitor.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Your name may follow your business, if you please.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : First light has almost found the sail on my page.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : The desk is quiet enough to entertain another voice.
line @5 greet [self.working=yes] : Allow me to finish this small upright stroke.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : For family I reserve a longer interval without an entry.
line @1 again.open : You've come round to a familiar page.
line @1 greet.return : A clear hail over the white margin.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : There's a voice that won't require a memorandum.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I heard while I was bringing the column down.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : I have the light and the leisure to listen.
line @1 farewell : May the day keep a little space unassigned for you.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll put that visit among my better expenditures.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Good light to your feet until your door.
line @1 react.news : What part of the account has been directly observed?
line @1 react.news.new : That's a detail I've yet to bring into the book.
line @1 react.news.known : I can find that entry on an earlier leaf.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Would that total survive inspection of the original notes?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I would suspend business with the household for a respectful interval.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I'd spare some of my best paper for such an entry.
line @1 answer.how : A little restless about matters absent from the day's account.
line @2 answer.how [self.working=yes] : Thoroughly occupied by things which can be counted.
line @1 ask.how : What have you enjoyed today beyond the ordinary figures?
line @1 sympathise : No entry has sufficient room for every sort of loss.
line @1 reassure : Take whatever part of the evening the matter asks.
line @1 decline : I'd have to break a proper undertaking at the yard to accept yours.
line @1 accept_decline : I shall leave my proposal in an unentered state.
line @1 thank : You have saved me a great many unnecessary figures.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Return the consideration to another patient reader.
line @1 preclose : My little ship is still waiting for a mast.
line @2 preclose [self.working=yes] : The yard requires the better part of this remaining light.
line @1 accept_preclose : Let's close the cover while there's a clear stopping place.
line @1 ack : Accounted.
scene ship
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a private book I draw one tiny ship for each evening I spend longing for a berth.
b : Are there many? | Do you give them all names?
a : A fleet by now, and very economical to maintain. | Only the ones whose sails look capable of carrying the vessel past the binding.

scene yard
when topic=work self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A yard account has room for pieces received, pieces used and pieces still needing explanation.
b : What sort of explanation? | Which figure do you enter first?
a : A sound block can become two smaller blocks between counting and laying. Arithmetic should allow the mason an occupation. | The one I've actually seen. The other two must wait their proper evidence.

scene stars
when topic=pastimes self.likes=stars
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave a narrow strip of sky above each ship in case the evening supplies a star.
b : What colour is the star? | Can it navigate?
a : The white of the paper. I surround it with a little wash and leave its centre untouched. | On the page the ship will go wherever the star is set. I'd rather like to test the opposite arrangement.

scene cakes
when topic=food self.likes=oatcakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An oatcake with a little butter is the least distracting meal I've found for a working day.
b : What if the butter gets on a page? | Do you eat at the desk?
a : It ceases to be an undistracting meal. I keep the saucer on the opposite side from the fresh paper. | At a short remove. Even a few paces can separate a respectable dinner from buttered accounts.

scene straw
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fresh straw has a different rustle from a floor merely swept over.
b : Is the sound clear from outside? | Do you like the rustle?
a : In a reasonably still room. A full gathering can drown out such a small economic fact. | I associate it with a place made ready before the first guest has had occasion to notice.

scene dawn
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A misty dawn lets the world take its shape a timber at a time.
b : Would you count in that light? | What appears first?
a : Only what's sufficiently near. A blurred number doesn't acquire authority by being entered early. | Usually a corner against clear sky. The grain follows later if I'm patient enough to stay.

scene flies
when topic=animals self.dislikes=flies
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fly once lent my private chart what looked like a small constellation.
b : Could you tell the stars apart? | Did you keep its contribution?
a : Under the glass six little prints proved remarkably symmetrical. | In the margin, with its authorship plainly indicated. The fly deserves whatever credit that brings.

scene haggle
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd prefer a price that can be explained to one which can be exhausted by argument.
b : Isn't that costly? | What makes a price explainable?
a : Waste half a working afternoon obtaining a discount and see what the discount's earned. | Material, labour and a plainly stated allowance. It needn't impersonate a miracle.

scene house
when topic=home self.house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can claim a house connection without claiming that I personally cut the stone the house supplied.
b : How would you describe your part? | Is the distinction important?
a : I enter the stone honestly and see that its use agrees with the book. | To the cutter with sore wrists, very much so. My columns don't blunt a chisel.

scene father
when topic=family self.father
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.father# the little sail in my margin before explaining why it's there.
b : Is it meant as a request? | Would you leave the book open?
a : As an opening to a conversation that outweighs a dinner engagement in my preferences. | I should stay to hear the answer. An unguarded sketch shouldn't be made to do all my speaking.

scene mother
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd take a clean copy of the best drawn ship to #self.mother#.
b : What would the gift say? | Would you include the price?
a : I'd hope the care given to the sail would speak adequately about the draughtsman. | None. That would defeat the entire purpose of keeping a private margin.

scene yardgate
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# a receipt must distinguish between the stone commissioned and the stone delivered to the actual yard.
b : Might they really differ? | Whose word counts?
a : A flaw may be found before delivery. I should like my book to represent the sound stone actually available. | I begin with the receiving count and let the commission explain why a difference matters.

scene shore
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like to go past a headland without having to enter its apparent size in any book.
b : Wouldn't you sketch it? | Where would you stand?
a : I probably would, later. First I should like the plain pleasure of seeing it dwindle. | Somewhere the crew didn't need space for a coil or a working foot. A berth doesn't confer expertise.

scene friend
when topic=smalltalk self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A blank page and an evening with #self.friend# might be a more profitable appointment than most of my formal calls.
b : Profit in what currency? | Why a blank page?
a : In being allowed to speak rather carelessly for once without anybody posting the results in a ledger. | If the conversation wanders, a private sketch can wander with it.

scene estate
when topic=home self.quarter=estate
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An estate dinner sometimes requires an extraordinary amount of scholarship concerning the order of a few plates.
b : Do you enjoy the ceremony? | Where would you rather be?
a : I enjoy the consideration if it makes the company easier. The plates themselves have limited social ambitions. | Just for one evening, near the water with my elbows arranged as I please.

scene road
when topic=lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A cargo acquires a surprising number of names between the quarry and a finished wall.
b : What names? | Which name's the proper one?
a : An order, a delivery, a receipt, a dressed stone. Only the last one can actually keep a roof up. | Each in its own column. The trick is remembering how many names one piece has earned.

scene coins
when topic=prices self.wealth=rich|comfortable
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can afford an excellent binding but a sound binding won't rescue a foolish account.
b : Would you keep it plain? | Why spend on it at all?
a : Durable and plain. Embossing can wait until my book has something worth keeping inside it. | Because a useful page deserves to survive the life of a cheap hinge.

scene dreamline
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sometimes try the first sentence of a letter written from a ship instead of from my desk.
b : What does it say? | Have you sent such a letter?
a : I should begin with a physical detail of the deck. No point travelling all that distance to report that I remain in good health. | Not yet. The address of the writer would be a slight obstacle at present.

scene newsink
when topic=news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A report from the water gets more interesting when its source describes what was visible from the deck.
b : Why ask about the view? | Would you trust a shore account?
a : I'm concerned with what was actually visible to the teller. | On a shore matter, very likely. Distance has a way of inserting a few attractive inaccuracies.

scene letterink
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A cost carried over twice can give two perfectly neat pages and a remarkably untidy conclusion.
b : How do you discover it? | Would you start again?
a : I follow one actual delivery across the joins until I've counted where each entry went. | With the smallest line first. Recopying the entire day may give the error a second fine set of clothes.

scene starpath
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At dusk the first star usually takes me by surprise when I lift my eyes from the page.
b : Can you predict the place? | Why does it surprise you?
a : Roughly. I still prefer to give the sky the courtesy of an inspection. | Because a black stroke made on paper asks for all the light I have, and a star requires me to let my eyes rest.

scene dust
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Stone dust has its own little ceremony before I touch a bound book.
b : What ceremony? | Why the binding especially?
a : Brush the coat outside, wash my palms, then see whether there's still chalk round the nails. | A loose leaf can be cleaned separately. Grit lodged in a hinge will do its work in private.

scene bell
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave one moment without an assignment when I hear a chapel bell between two yard errands.
b : Do you stop completely? | Is a moment sufficient?
a : If the errand allows. Otherwise I can listen without turning the sound into another item to be collected. | For being reminded of the things my books leave out, yes.

scene guest
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A traveller who has sailed past our headland has already brought me a subject for dinner.
b : Would you ask about trade? | How many questions would you ask?
a : After hearing about the sea itself. I've a desk full of information on the commercial face of water. | Fewer than my curiosity might suggest. A guest deserves a mouthful of oatcake between adventures.

scene shapes
when topic=land
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A line drawn for a horizon must be straighter than a line drawn to add my figures.
b : Is the sea straight? | What if your hand wavers?
a : At a great distance it seems to me to possess an enviably steady edge. | A distant wave has arrived on my private sheet. I shall exercise mercy towards my draughtsman.

scene paperwind
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When a breeze lifts a corner of my paper I am tempted to give it a mast.
b : Would the paper sail? | What holds the paper down?
a : Beautifully across the desk and quite poorly on the water. Ink has limited sea legs. | A squared sample of stone. It earns its keep more effectively here than afloat.

scene innminute
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I am too easily persuaded to linger where sailors sit after an evening's work.
b : Do you ever exchange a word? | Is the appeal the drink?
a : If they have time for a listener with precise questions and singularly little practice at sea. | The conversation. One moderate cup can last me the whole of a well-told passage.

story standing [topic=work self.job=merchant]
  : I found a short length of timber entered as a full beam and went to see how much had gone astray.
  : Two shorter lengths laid together matched the original beam's dimensions almost exactly.
  b : Was the account wrong?
  : The quantity was honest and the description required amendment. A roof has particular opinions about a join midway across a room.

story flysky [topic=pastimes]
  : A fly landed on my little ship while the ink was damp and walked across the empty sky.
  : I followed its footprints with a glass and found four almost convincing stars in a neat row.
  b : Did you draw the fifth?
  : No. Nature had put in a day's work without a commission, and I resolved to preserve its individual style.

story butterboat [topic=food]
  : I cut a pat of butter so thinly it curled up like a sail on the warm oatcake.
  : It was the best little rig I'd made all week until the bottom began to melt away.
  b : Did the voyage finish?
  : Across the plate and no further. It was a short but unusually satisfactory passage.

story strawdeck [topic=dreams]
  : I laid some lengths of fresh straw across a private account to see what a ship's deck would look like in miniature.
  : The long stems hid the sums and left the whole margin visible, which I found a rather attractive arrangement.
  b : Did you keep the deck?
  : I sketched its proportions and restored the sums. A yard still has to get paid on my imaginary sailing days.

story mistedge [topic=weather]
  : At dawn I mistook a corner of roof rising through the mist for the bow of a vessel.
  : A moment's extra light gave it a chimney, two gutters and some very permanent stone supports.
  b : Were you disappointed?
  : Only until I had drawn the original mistaken outline. A little inaccuracy can make an excellent private ship.

rule @tally
when concept=bark self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Delivered pieces in the near column, please. | Mind the distinction between orders and receipts.

rule @stars
when concept=bark self.likes=stars
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A fresh star for the private fleet. | Keep that corner of the margin blank.

rule @cakes
when concept=bark self.likes=oatcakes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Butter well away from the new paper. | A thin curl for the second oatcake.

rule @mist
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Even the yard gate looks afloat at present. | Wait for the roof to recover its edges.

rule @flies
when concept=bark self.dislikes=flies
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The fly has no account to enter here. | Cover the wet star chart.

rule @wind
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A stone weight for the foot of the page. | My paper ship is trying the air.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I have a private margin with a little room for an unexpected conversation.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You've seen the little vessel in the margin, #topic.player#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : The public account is available. My other pages will stay closed.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=night] : The lamp gives us a circle of paper and the window supplies a patch of sky.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=merchant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I reconcile the entries with materials somebody can actually build with.
dlg @2 resident.job : I know what a sheet can tell us about a load and where the sheet must yield to the load itself.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : One entry newly reached my desk. #world.news#.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : The subject of #world.event_words# may affect today's returns.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : Nothing on that subject has been made public in my hearing.
dlg @1 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare] : There are articles available to inspect. I'll give the figures for the particular piece that interests you.
dlg @2 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : No stock to offer today. A sensible enquiry may still earn a sensible answer.
dlg @1 shop.prices : I'd look at numbers and goods together before discussing terms.
dlg @1 shop.bye : May your purchase give as honest an account of itself in use.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Leave the day's last corner open to a view past the roofs.
graft @fleetmargin resident.hub
choice What's the little sail beside the figures? -> fleetmargin
node fleetmargin
say A private entry. It records an evening when I'd sooner have been standing on a real deck than adding up materials for something built on land.
choice Does it carry any cargo? -> fleetmargin_more
choice Close the private page. -> hub
node fleetmargin_more
say A single white star and the prospect of going further next time. That's plenty of freight for a vessel my smallest finger could cover.
choice Close the private page. -> hub
choice Return to the yard. -> bye

graft @unpriced resident.hub
choice Is this the only unpriced thing on your desk? -> unpriced
node unpriced
say The sail has company. My view through the window and a conversation freely offered have likewise escaped a written valuation.
choice Would you put a price on a real berth? -> unpriced_more
choice Look back at the page. -> hub
node unpriced_more
say Gladly, if the terms included a chance to earn my place aboard. A paid view is a different matter from a voyage I helped to finish.
choice Look back at the page. -> hub
choice Leave the window clear. -> bye
